From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:30:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] extmod/modos: keep the input os.dupterm_notify() has no room
 for.

os.dupterm_notify() moves every character a dupterm stream holds into
stdin_ringbuf, and ringbuf_put() drops each one that doesn't fit. On the
esp32 port, WebREPL's socket calls it whenever a poll finds the socket
readable, and that can be right after a timer callback has run inside
the REPL's wait for input. A command that arrived in one piece during
the callback, as a raw-REPL command does from a tool that doesn't use
raw-paste, is then cut to what fits in the buffer plus whatever arrives
later: the REPL runs a broken command, or never sees its Ctrl-D and the
tool waits for its timeout.

While the REPL waits for input no interrupt character is set, and a
port whose mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() reads the dupterm streams once
stdin_ringbuf is empty doesn't need the rest read early. The new option
MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL makes os.dupterm_notify()
stop at a full buffer then and leave the rest in the stream. While code
runs it keeps reading as before, so that a Ctrl-C behind a full buffer
still interrupts it. The option is off by default and on for esp32.
rp2 and mimxrt read their streams the same way but haven't been tried
with it. esp8266 must leave it off: its mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() reads
only stdin_ringbuf, so the rest would wait for the next packet.
---
 extmod/modos.c             | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/extmod/modos.c b/extmod/modos.c
index c330162..3d4e2d4 100644
--- a/extmod/modos.c
+++ b/extmod/modos.c
@@ -60,6 +60,20 @@
 #include "genhdr/mpversion.h"
 #endif
 
+#if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY
+// A port whose mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() reads the dupterm streams itself once
+// stdin_ringbuf is empty can set this to 1. os.dupterm_notify() then stops
+// at a full buffer while no interrupt character is set, as while the REPL
+// waits for input, and what doesn't fit stays in its stream instead of
+// being dropped.
+#ifndef MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL
+#define MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL (0)
+#endif
+#if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL
+#include "shared/runtime/interrupt_char.h"
+#endif
+#endif
+
 #ifdef MICROPY_PY_OS_INCLUDEFILE
 #include MICROPY_PY_OS_INCLUDEFILE
 #endif
@@ -134,6 +148,15 @@ static MP_DEFINE_CONST_FUN_OBJ_0(mp_os_uname_obj, mp_os_uname);
 static mp_obj_t mp_os_dupterm_notify(mp_obj_t obj_in) {
     (void)obj_in;
     for (;;) {
+        #if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL
+        // A character read with no room left in stdin_ringbuf is lost. While
+        // the REPL waits for input, leave the rest in the stream for
+        // mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() to read. While code runs, keep reading so
+        // that a Ctrl-C behind a full buffer still interrupts it.
+        if (mp_interrupt_char < 0 && ringbuf_free(&stdin_ringbuf) == 0) {
+            break;
+        }
+        #endif
         int c = mp_os_dupterm_rx_chr();
         if (c < 0) {
             break;
diff --git a/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h b/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
index ecdc4b2..f73514f 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
+++ b/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@
 #define MICROPY_PY_RANDOM_SEED_INIT_FUNC    (esp_random())
 #define MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM               (1)
 #define MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY        (1)
+#define MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY_STOP_WHEN_FULL (1)
 #define MICROPY_PY_OS_SYNC                  (1)
 #define MICROPY_PY_OS_UNAME                 (1)
 #define MICROPY_PY_OS_URANDOM               (1)
-- 
